  "Another Sunspear confession reaches camp, this one naming Riverlands notables who took Dornish coin to sabotage relief roads while denouncing foreign influence in public. Arya wants the names posted at every crossroads. Beric cautions that half the list may be bait designed to start civil reprisals.

Edited versions of the confession are already in circulation, each one accusing a different faction. A public release can reclaim narrative control if evidence holds. A covert verification phase can prevent false purges but may look like a cover-up when hunger crowds the courts. In this climate, delayed truth can be as deadly as lies.

Vigil lamps flicker over rows of marked graves. Your next move decides whether justice is immediate and risky, or careful and politically expensive."

