section__
  @title "The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/02-act2-riverlands/frame-119.jpg"

  "At Trident dock stores, salt quotas collapse after several tax riders are found dead with forged warrants pinned to their cloaks. Beric argues for a transparent crackdown before looting spreads. Arya argues the forgeries came from inside at least one allied keep, and public accusations without proof could detonate the coalition.

Quartermasters now assign food by secured district, effectively turning policy into a map of who commands fear. If you respond in open court, you may restore trust while exposing just how compromised your apparatus is. If you settle accounts through covert blackmail, supplies may flow again tomorrow with legality reduced to a prop.

River wind rattles stained sept glass while carts queue for salt. The Riverlands can survive hypocrisy for a season, but not disorder."

