section__
  @title "Riverrun Broken Oath under rain"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/02-act2-riverlands/frame-120.jpg"

  "Riverrun's floodplain is a sheet of mud and burned grain when a coalition of minor lords demands proof that Valehart can enforce one coherent ration policy across their lands. Edmure presses for a formal oath renewal at dawn. Sandor warns that one more public ceremony without immediate security will look like weakness dressed as law.

Several houses threaten to fracture if you do not decide now between strict public allocation, covert coercion, or foreign-backed acceleration. Delay is no longer neutral; every postponed order becomes another village choosing its own militia and tolls. The act closes with no clean outcomes left, only clearer costs.

You taste smoke, river salt, and rain as scribes set final orders. What you choose here determines how Act 2 hands its wounds to the Northward campaign."

